The baselines are summarized in the upper part of the results table. One of them is "Balikas et al.", the winning system of the 2016 edition of the challenge, which is believed to hold the state of the art [1].

The multitask approach was also compared with several other models [2]:
- an SVM with a linear kernel and a one-vs-rest approach for the multi-class problem [2];
- an SVM with a linear kernel using the Crammer-Singer strategy [2];
- logistic regression with a one-vs-rest approach [2];
- multinomial logistic regression, also known as the MaxEnt classifier [2].

The excerpts do not say explicitly which of these models are the table's baselines, apart from "Balikas et al." [1].
